      "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ for $y=7x-4{x}^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7x-4{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =7-2\\cdot 4x \\\\  & =7-8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7-8x) \\\\  & =0-8 \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
